course: dictionary
lesson: 14969
title: Remnants: what is left behind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A remnant is a small part of something that is left after the rest has gone or been used. Look for clue words like «left» and «after» in the sentence. «Only a few remnants of the meal were left on the plates.» The meal has been eaten, and the small bits that remain are the remnants.
explain: Remnant can also mean a piece of cloth left over from a big roll, often sold cheaply. «The shop sold fabric remnants for a pound each.» The shop is selling the leftover pieces, not whole rolls.
explain: Remnants can also be small parts that have survived from long ago. «We found remnants of an old Roman wall in the field.» The wall is not whole any more, but a few pieces of it are still there.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a few small bits that are left» fit in «the remnants of the meal»? If it does, you have understood the word.
fact: A remnant is a small part that is left after the rest has gone or been used.
fact: «Remnants» is the plural: one remnant, many remnants.
fact: In maths, a remnant is like a remainder: a 10 m roll cut into 3 m pieces leaves a 1 m remnant.
fact: A fabric remnant is a leftover piece of cloth, often sold cheaply in shops.
fact: «The remnants of» is a common phrase, as in «the remnants of an old forest».
exercise: «Only a few remnants of the meal were left on the plates.» What are the remnants? | The big, full dishes | *The small bits left after the meal | The plates bought last year | The guests who came late
exercise: A 10 m roll of fabric is cut into 3 m pieces. What is the 1 m piece left over called? | A 10 m roll | *A remnant | A 3 m piece | A full roll
exercise: «We found remnants of an old Roman wall in the field.» What do the remnants show? | *Small surviving parts of something old | A field full of sheep | A new wall being built | A party with lots of food
test: «The shop sold fabric remnants for a pound each.» In this sentence, a remnant is a piece of what? | Water from a river | Sand from a beach | Metal from a bridge | *Cloth left over from a roll
test: Which phrase means a small part that survives from the past? | a new roll of cloth | a full meal | a sunny day | *a remnant of the past
exam: Which word is the plural of remnant? | *remnants | remnantly | remnanting | remnant's
